      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in most labeling.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. They add no glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose:** tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise I'll enter the corrected order once you pick one."
      }
     ],
